articles.content_en:
To initiate an environmental civil public interest litigation, the following materials shall be submitted:
(1) a statement of complaint conforming to the provisions of Article 121 of the Civil Procedure Law, and copies submitted in accordance with the number of defendants;
(2) preliminary evidentiary materials proving that the defendant's act has already harmed the social public interest or has a major risk of harming the social public interest;
(3) where the lawsuit is initiated by a social organization, it shall submit its social organization registration certificate, articles of association, annual work reports or annual inspection reports for the five consecutive years prior to the initiation of the lawsuit, and a declaration of no record of violations of law signed by its legal representative or person in charge and affixed with the official seal.

Where the plaintiff requests the defendant to bear the following expenses, the People's Court may support the request in accordance with law:
(1) expenses for investigation, expert evaluation and assessment of ecological environment damage;
(2) reasonable expenses incurred for cleaning up pollution and preventing the occurrence and expansion of damage;
(3) reasonable attorney fees and other reasonable expenses incurred for the litigation.
